  "design": {
    "e_data": "mean squared in-sample prediction error in metric units; basis-independent, scored at full precision. Pdiag finite must degrade in rotated bases; the Full operator and the provably Ad-invariant Frame-weighted scalar must not.",
    "rescaling_floor": "closed-form best-achievable e_alpha for any diagonal model in a rotated basis: proj_k(s) = sum_j A[k,j] R[j,k] d_j(s) with A = C0'^-1 C0_true ~ I, i.e. the rescaled law d_k(s) * R[k,k]. The fitted e_alpha(rotated) exceeds it because the pose6-weighted objective contorts the diagonal to chase the off-diagonal response (a law-vs-data tension that only exists off the task basis)."
  },
